Z||000001||Mach10||10-19-2001||12:56 AM||||Well, as far as I know, the z34 only ever came in a 3.4TDC motor... Big car, fairly powerful motor. Don't have any hard numbers, but I don't think it's any faster than a Fiero. The one I drove didn't feel faster, anyway. Nice cars though. Sharp, and of course, that motor has a nice shriek of rage sound  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||Formula88||10-19-2001||09:24 AM||||Correct, Z34's only came with the 3.4DOHC engine.  It was rated between 205 and 215HP depending on year.  I'd love to find one of those or a GTP with that engine and a 5 speed.  That'd be the perfect daily driver for a Fiero owner!  <P>Be warned, though.  That's a high maintenance engine.  Very complex oiling system.  You have to make sure you change the oil every 3K miles religiously - I'd recommend only a good quality synthetic oil, too.  ||||reg||1
